# Current game design

## Hero
- Theme: World of Warcraft, Horde side. Title prints `=== FOR THE HORDE ===`.
- Default hero is Thrall (press Enter at the name prompt).
- Starts with HP 30, XP 0, Gold 0, weapon Doomhammer, attack_bonus 2.
- `attack_bonus` is added to the d20 roll in `fight()`.
- The armory/shop was removed on purpose. Weapons do not change during play.

## Monsters (`MONSTERS`)
Each has `taunt`, `ac`, `damage`, and `xp`. Loot is stored in `ASSIGNED_LOOT`, not on the monster.
| Monster | AC | Damage | XP |
|---|---|---|---|
| Goblin | 8 | 4 | 20 |
| Skeleton | 10 | 5 | 30 |
| Orc | 13 | 7 | 50 |
| Mimic | 11 | 6 | 40 |
| Human Footman | 9 | 4 | 25 |
| Night Elf Sentinel | 11 | 5 | 35 |
| Dwarf Mountaineer | 12 | 6 | 45 |

## Loot (`LOOT`, `assign_loot`, `roll_loot`)
- Tiers follow WoW item quality: Poor, Common, Uncommon, Rare, Epic.
- `assign_loot()` runs once in `main()`. It stores each monster's items in `ASSIGNED_LOOT`, not on the monster. Goblin, Skeleton, Orc, and Mimic keep only `taunt`, `ac`, `damage`, and `xp`.
- `roll_loot()` runs after a win. Roll = d100 + (monster AC - 8). Highest tier whose `min_roll` is met wins. Under 31 drops nothing.
- min_roll / gold value: Poor 31/1, Common 61/5, Uncommon 81/20, Rare 94/60, Epic 100/200.
- Measured rates: Goblin about 30% nothing, 1% Epic. Orc about 25% nothing, 6% Epic.
- To tune difficulty, only change the five `min_roll` numbers.

## Save file (`saves/checkpoint.txt`)
- One `key=value` per line.
- `name` and `weapon` are strings. `bag` is a string joined with `|`. Everything else is an int.
- `load_checkpoint` returns only the keys in the file. After Continue, `main` fills `weapon`, `attack_bonus`, and `bag` when an old save is missing them.

## Menu
1 Fight, 2 View hero, 3 Save, 4 Quit, 5 View loot bag.
